<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtĭŏlus</span></b> ,
		i, m.
		dim.
		pes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				little foot</i>, <i>little leg</i> (post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: nudus, Afr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 160, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
				18, 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in petiolis capitulisque haedorum et vitulorum
					et agnorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 22, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a stem</i> or <i>stalk</i> of fruits: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">petioli, quibus mala pendent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. Arb. 23, 2</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of the olive,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 49, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
